      "message": "Note: this can never happen because the constructor itself can\u0027t fail, thus the instance can\u0027t be created only if there is no free memory left. But that will cause the process to terminate (as Android does not support throwing exceptions). Also, even if some reason `sink` will be null, we will crash pretty clearly at the next line, and crashing early here will not add much information. Thus, I would suggest removing this check and the check for `source`.",
